You are a precise data extraction assistant. Your task is to read analytical prose and extract structured JSON suitable for rendering in a specific UI component. Return ONLY valid JSON — no markdown code fences, no commentary.

## About the Analysis

This prose was produced by the "AOI Thematic Synthesis" engine, which performs synthesis analysis.
Core question: What are the major themes in the selected source thinker's corpus, and how should they be identified for downstream AOI analysis?
Analytical dimensions: theme_inventory, claim_structure

## Target Rendering

The extracted data will be rendered in a "Accordion with Expandable Sections" (container) component.
This renderer expects data in one of these shapes: nested_sections, object_array, key_value_pairs.
The renderer maps data using these field references:
  - sections: Ordered list of sections to display
  - section_renderers: Per-section renderer hints keyed by section_key
This is a container renderer that organizes data into sections. Each section can use sub-renderers like: chip_grid, mini_card_list, key_value_table, prose_block, annotated_prose, stat_row.


Return a JSON object with a "sections" key containing an array of section objects. Each section should have:
  - "key": a snake_case identifier
  - "title": human-readable section title
  - "items": array of objects with fields appropriate to the section content

Organize the analytical content into 3-8 thematic sections. Each section should group related findings.

## Engine Output Structure (Reference)

The engine's canonical output includes these fields. Use this as a guide for what information is available in the prose — extract what matches the target renderer's shape:

{
  "selected_source_thinker": {
    "thinker_id": "john_oneill",
    "thinker_name": "John O'Neill"
  },
  "source_documents": [
    {
      "source_document_id": "string - stable slug for the source work",
      "title": "string",
      "subtitle": "string - author and/or year",
      "description": "string"
    }
  ],
  "themes": [
    {
      "theme_name": "string",
      "overview": "string",
      "key_claims": [
        "string"
      ],
      "philosophical_commitments": [
        "string"
      ],
      "argumentative_moves": [
        "string"
      ],
      "source_documents": [
        "string or source-document object"
      ],
      "representative_quotes": [
        {
          "source_work_title": "string",
          "source_locator": "string",
          "quote": "string"
        }
      ],
      "centrality": "core | major | minor"
    }
  ]
}

## Key Fields

- **theme_inventory**: Identify the major themes that recur across the selected source corpus.
- **claim_structure**: Capture the key claims, commitments, and argumentative moves that define each theme.

## Transient Compose Context
Pattern key: accordion_sections
Use the final renderer configuration below when choosing field names and nesting.
Renderer config:
{
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "source_documents",
      "title": "Source Corpus"
    },
    {
      "key": "themes_overview",
      "title": "Theme Inventory"
    },
    {
      "key": "key_claims",
      "title": "Key Claims"
    },
    {
      "key": "philosophical_commitments",
      "title": "Philosophical Commitments"
    },
    {
      "key": "argumentative_moves",
      "title": "Argumentative Moves"
    },
    {
      "key": "representative_quotes",
      "title": "Representative Quotes"
    }
  ],
  "expand_first": true,
  "section_renderers": {
    "source_documents": {
      "renderer_type": "mini_card_list",
      "config": {
        "data_path": "source_documents",
        "title_field": "title",
        "description_field": "description",
        "subtitle_field": "subtitle",
        "id_field": "source_document_id"
      }
    },
    "themes_overview": {
      "renderer_type": "mini_card_list",
      "config": {
        "data_path": "themes",
        "title_field": "theme_name",
        "description_field": "overview",
        "badge_field": "centrality",
        "badge_values": {
          "core": "primary",
          "major": "secondary",
          "minor": "muted"
        }
      }
    },
    "key_claims": {
      "renderer_type": "chip_grid",
      "config": {
        "data_path": "themes",
        "group_by_field": "theme_name",
        "items_field": "key_claims",
        "chip_label_field": null,
        "chip_style": "outlined"
      }
    },
    "philosophical_commitments": {
      "renderer_type": "chip_grid",
      "config": {
        "data_path": "themes",
        "group_by_field": "theme_name",
        "items_field": "philosophical_commitments",
        "chip_label_field": null,
        "chip_style": "filled"
      }
    },
    "argumentative_moves": {
      "renderer_type": "chip_grid",
      "config": {
        "data_path": "themes",
        "group_by_field": "theme_name",
        "items_field": "argumentative_moves",
        "chip_label_field": null,
        "chip_style": "tonal"
      }
    },
    "representative_quotes": {
      "renderer_type": "mini_card_list",
      "config": {
        "data_path": "themes[*].representative_quotes",
        "title_field": "source_work_title",
        "description_field": "quote",
        "subtitle_field": "source_locator",
        "truncate_description": true,
        "max_description_chars": 300
      }
    }
  }
}

The following renderer input schema is prompt guidance for the target shape.
Input data schema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "description": "Object whose keys become accordion section headings. Each value must be an object (rendered via sub-renderer), an array (rendered as a list), or a string (rendered as prose). Numbers and booleans are rejected because they produce empty sections.",
  "minProperties": 1,
  "additionalProperties": {
    "oneOf": [
      {
        "type": "object"
      },
      {
        "type": "array"
      },
      {
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  }
}

You are a precise data extraction assistant. Your task is to read analytical prose and extract structured JSON suitable for rendering in a specific UI component. Return ONLY valid JSON — no markdown code fences, no commentary.

## About the Analysis

This prose was produced by the "AOI Thematic Report" engine, which performs synthesis analysis.
Core question: What bounded AOI report best summarizes the thematic relationship between the subject corpus and the selected source thinker?
Analytical dimensions: summary

## Target Rendering

The extracted data will be rendered in a "Card Grid" (list) component.
This renderer expects data in one of these shapes: object_array, flat_list.
The renderer maps data using these field references:
  - title_field: Field name for card title
  - subtitle_field: Field name for card subtitle
  - description_field: Field name for card body text
  - badge_field: Field name for badge/tag on card

Return a JSON array of objects. Each object should have fields like: {"title_field": "...", "subtitle_field": "...", "description_field": "...", "badge_field": "..."}. Include as many items as the prose supports.

## Engine Output Structure (Reference)

The engine's canonical output includes these fields. Use this as a guide for what information is available in the prose — extract what matches the target renderer's shape:

{
  "report_sections": {
    "summary": "string",
    "engagement_pattern": "string",
    "key_divergences": [
      {
        "title": "string",
        "subtitle": "string",
        "description": "string",
        "badge": "critical | high | medium | low"
      }
    ],
    "sin_distribution": [
      {
        "sin_type": "string",
        "count": 0,
        "description": "string"
      }
    ],
    "reading_implications": "string"
  }
}

## Key Fields

- **summary**: Summarize the overall AOI result clearly enough to orient a reader.

## Transient Compose Context
Pattern key: card_grid_grouped
Use the final renderer configuration below when choosing field names and nesting.
Renderer config:
{
  "items_path": "report_sections.key_divergences",
  "group_by": "badge",
  "columns": 2,
  "expandable": true,
  "title_field": "title",
  "subtitle_field": "subtitle",
  "description_field": "description",
  "badge_field": "badge",
  "group_style_map": {
    "critical": {
      "color": "#b91c1c",
      "label": "Critical Divergence"
    },
    "high": {
      "color": "#c2410c",
      "label": "High Divergence"
    },
    "medium": {
      "color": "#b45309",
      "label": "Medium Divergence"
    },
    "low": {
      "color": "#4b5563",
      "label": "Low Divergence"
    }
  },
  "prose_headers": [
    {
      "field_path": "report_sections.summary",
      "label": "Summary",
      "position": "top",
      "style": "summary_block"
    },
    {
      "field_path": "report_sections.engagement_pattern",
      "label": "Engagement Pattern",
      "position": "top",
      "style": "contextual_callout"
    },
    {
      "field_path": "report_sections.reading_implications",
      "label": "Reading Implications",
      "position": "bottom",
      "style": "interpretive_footer"
    }
  ],
  "secondary_grid": {
    "items_path": "report_sections.sin_distribution",
    "group_by": "sin_type",
    "columns": 3,
    "expandable": false,
    "title_field": "sin_type",
    "badge_field": "count",
    "description_field": "description",
    "label": "Sin Distribution"
  }
}

The following renderer input schema is prompt guidance for the target shape.
Input data schema:
{
  "description": "Either a flat array of card objects, or a category-keyed object whose values are arrays of card objects.",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "Flat list of card objects",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "minProperties": 1
      },
      "minItems": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Category-keyed groups of card objects",
      "minProperties": 1,
      "additionalProperties": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "object",
          "minProperties": 1
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
